grid: the Grid command line

Usage: grid <command> [flags]

Commands:
  version     print the CLI, contract and app_min versions
  where       show which project and task a folder belongs to
  open        open the task page in the browser
  doctor      check machine health and collect a support bundle
  hook        answer a Claude Code or Codex hook event; set and list hook levels
  task        new, show, list, status, lane, stop|close|reopen, history, attach, move, decline, delete, rename, restore
  plan        write, check, items, hash, diff, migrate
  job         next, post, ack, result, cancel, tree, blocked, render, lint, show, verify, cycles, order, trace
  lease       take, release, status (task lease)
  feed        tick, post, read, state, types, handover, fold
  mcp         stdio server with the Feed tools
  question    add, ask, withdraw, list, tick and sync task questions
  answer      record a person's answer
  approve     approve the plan or a later approve step (a person or the app only)
  deliver     write the outcome and wait for the person
  proof       add evidence and rebuild the task proof index
  history     add a dated line to the task history
  land        land a task per the deploy topic
  brain       show, search, topics, index, propose, accept, keep, decide, supersede, check, changes, revert
  env         up, down browser Job dev environments
  person      check person access; list, show and find approvers
  routine     add, list, remove, run, schedule and unschedule routines
  worker      list local grid-worker processes; next is a worker's call for its next request
  agent       check agent readiness; sync templates; set or unset models and efforts; budget; list settings
  claude      show and set the person's Claude Code settings rows
  workflow    show workflow template files and parse problems; write a template file
  skill       enable, disable and list skills
  session     list, show, start, stop, send, pause, resume, handback, switch
  intent      list, claim, done, release, renew (worker requests)
  usage       post and show usage, fold observed session totals
  account     list, status, statusline, scan, sign-in, windows, folder and note for agent accounts
  project     add, remove, list, scan and relink projects; repo edits a project's repos
  project-md  get or set a project front-matter key
  setup       record project setup answers and write the Claude Code settings block (--sandbox turns on its sandbox)
  signal      add, act on, dismiss and move inbox signals
  artifact    import, link, list and publish task artifacts
  eval        list, run and show task evaluations; export-suite writes plugin eval cases
  migrate     upgrade the Grid home to this format

Global flags go before the command; each wins over its environment variable:
  --grid-home DIR    the Grid home (GRID_HOME)
  --member ID        who is calling (GRID_MEMBER)
  --role ROLE        the caller's role (GRID_ROLE)
  --lease-epoch G.F  the lease generation.fence (GRID_LEASE_EPOCH)

Exit status: 0 done, 1 failed, 2 usage, 3 rejected (stale lease, invalid record or intent claim token; do not retry), 4 disk full, 5 taken (intent already claimed or done; skip).
